Explicitly excluded: hyper-compress-wasm and Kura (separately licensed by the
BentoPDF authors; not redistributed here). At upstream v2.8.10 no source file
imports hyper-compress-wasm (grep of src/ and package.json/package-lock.json
finds none); only the kura.html and hyper-compress.html marketing pages exist,
and scripts/build-local.sh deletes them from the bundle and fails the build if
they or the string "hyper-compress-wasm" reappear (scripts/check-dist.sh).
Links to those pages from navbar/legal pages are not removed.

No release artifact ships while any line above is still marked as unresolved. Enforced by
packaging/check-notice.sh --release and by `packaging/verify-artifact.sh --release` (tag builds).

Corresponding source for any distributed artifact:
  - This project: this repository at the commit recorded in the bundle's SOURCE.txt, plus the pinned
    upstream BentoPDF tag and commit recorded in UPSTREAM_VERSION and UPSTREAM_COMMIT. Every built bundle
    contains SOURCE.txt, LICENSE and this NOTICE.
  - @bentopdf/pymupdf-wasm 0.11.16 (modified PyMuPDF): package.json repository
    https://github.com/alam00000/bentopdf-pymupdf-wasm.git ; its README: "The source code for this package is
    available at: https://github.com/alam00000/bentopdf-pymupdf-wasm" and the package carries build_scripts/.
  - @bentopdf/gs-wasm 0.1.1 (modified Ghostscript): package.json repository
    https://github.com/alam00000/bentopdf-gs-wasm.git ; same README statement, with build_scripts/.
  - coherentpdf 2.5.5: package.json repository https://github.com/coherentgraphics/coherentpdf.js.git
    (homepage https://github.com/coherentgraphics/coherentpdf.js#readme). Its README states no separate
    source location for the compiled JavaScript: NEEDS REVIEW (corresponding source of the shipped
    coherentpdf.js build not identified).
  - bentopdf-pdfium (AGPL-3.0): package.json declares no repository or homepage. The upstream workflow
    .github/workflows/update-bentopdf-viewer.yml packs prebuilt packages/pdfium/src/vendor/pdfium.{js,wasm}
    from https://github.com/alam00000/bentopdf-pdfium-viewer (branch main) into the vendor/ tarball; the
    tarball holds only editcore.js, editcore.wasm and package.json. How that wasm was built, and its
    source, is not shown by those files: NEEDS REVIEW (corresponding source of the pdfium engine).
  - LibreOffice WASM build (MPL-2.0): see the LibreOffice engine line above; remains NEEDS REVIEW there.
  - Flatpak GPL/LGPL base libraries: see the Electron Flatpak runtime line above.
  - FFmpeg in Electron/Chromium: see the Chromium line above.

